To enhance the "Jump and Run" game by adding images, we'll replace the colored blocks with images for the player and the obstacle. Below is a modified version of the previous code where we incorporate images.

Make sure you have the images you want to use saved in the same directory as your HTML file. For this example, I'll assume you have:

- `player.png` for the player character.
- `obstacle.png` for the obstacle.

### HTML (index.html)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Jump and Run Game</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
    <div class="game-container">
        <div class="player" id="player"></div>
        <div class="ground"></div>
        <div class="obstacle" id="obstacle"></div>
    </div>
    <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

### CSS (styles.css)

```css
* {
    box-sizing: border-box;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
}

body {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    height: 100vh;
    background: #87CEEB; /* Sky background color */
}

.game-container {
    position: relative;
    width: 600px;
    height: 300px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background-color: #8B4513; /* Brown ground */
}

.player {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 20px;
    left: 50px;
    width: 50px; /* Adjusted to match image size */
    height: 50px; /* Adjusted to match image size */
    background-image: url('player.png');
    background-size: cover; /* Ensure the image fills the div */
}

.ground {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 20px;
    background-color: #654321; /* Ground color */
}

.obstacle {
    position: absolute;
    bottom: 20px;
    right: 0;
    width: 50px; /* Adjusted to match image size */
    height: 50px; /* Adjusted to match image size */
    background-image: url('obstacle.png');
    background-size: cover; /* Ensure the image fills the div */
}
```

### JavaScript (script.js)

```javascript
const player = document.getElementById('player');
const obstacle = document.getElementById('obstacle');

let isJumping = false;
let isGameOver = false;

// Function to handle player jumping
function jump() {
    if (isJumping) return;
    isJumping = true;

    let jumpHeight = 0;
    const jumpInterval = setInterval(() => {
        if (jumpHeight >= 100) {
            clearInterval(jumpInterval);
            fall();
        } else {
            jumpHeight += 5;
            player.style.bottom = `${20 + jumpHeight}px`;
        }
    }, 20);
}

// Function to handle player falling
function fall() {
    let fallHeight = 100;
    const fallInterval = setInterval(() => {
        if (fallHeight <= 0) {
            clearInterval(fallInterval);
            isJumping = false;
        } else {
            fallHeight -= 5;
            player.style.bottom = `${20 + fallHeight}px`;
        }
    }, 20);
}

// Function to handle game over
function checkCollision() {
    const playerRect = player.getBoundingClientRect();
    const obstacleRect = obstacle.getBoundingClientRect();

    if (
        playerRect.x < obstacleRect.x + obstacleRect.width &&
        playerRect.x + playerRect.width > obstacleRect.x &&
        playerRect.y < obstacleRect.y + obstacleRect.height &&
        playerRect.y + playerRect.height > obstacleRect.y
    ) {
        alert('Game Over!');
        clearInterval(obstacleMove);
        isGameOver = true;
    }
}

// Move the obstacle
let obstacleMove = setInterval(() => {
    if (isGameOver) return;

    let obstaclePosition = parseInt(window.getComputedStyle(obstacle).getPropertyValue('right'));
    obstaclePosition += 2;
    if (obstaclePosition > 600) {
        obstaclePosition = 0; // Reset position
    }
    obstacle.style.right = `${obstaclePosition}px`;
    checkCollision();
}, 20);

// Listen for keydown events to jump
document.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
    if (event.code === 'Space') {
        jump();
    }
});
```

### Images

Make sure you have two images named `player.png` and `obstacle.png` in the same directory as your HTML file. You can use any images you like for the player and the obstacle.

1. **Player Image**: This should be a small character or figure.
2. **Obstacle Image**: This could be a block, a cactus, or any other obstacle image you'd like.

### Adjusting Image Sizes
Adjust the dimensions in the CSS if your images are not 50x50 pixels. You can change the `width` and `height` properties of the `.player` and `.obstacle` classes to match your images.

### Test Your Game
1. Save the changes to the HTML, CSS, and JavaScript files.
2. Ensure your images are in the directory.
3. Open the `index.html` file in a web browser to test the game. Press the `Space` key to jump over the falling obstacles.

Now you should have a working "Jump and Run" game with images! Enjoy enhancing it further!